            "intro": "",
            "question_1": "How much can the rear rack hold?",
            "answer_1": "Both Kodiak and Kodiak V2 rear racks are rated for up to 120 lb of cargo. Total rider-plus-cargo payload is 300 lb. Do not exceed either limit.",
            "question_2": "What motor and range do I get?",
            "answer_2": "Both use a Bafang 500W (750W peak) hub motor with 80 Nm torque and a 32 km/h top speed. Listed range: 80–100+ km (Kodiak) and 100+ km (Kodiak V2). Heavy cargo, hills, cold weather, and high assist levels reduce range.",
            "question_3": "Is there a BC rebate?",
